# Python Project: Book Scraper and Price Analysis

A web scraping and data analysis pipeline. It collects book data from [books.toscrape.com](https://books.toscrape.com) (a public site made for scraping practice), cleans it with pandas, and analyses how price relates to star rating.

## What it does
- Scrapes title, price, star rating and stock status with `requests` and `BeautifulSoup`.
- Handles request errors and waits between requests to be polite to the server.
- Cleans the data (extracts numeric prices, converts rating words to numbers, removes duplicates).
- Saves `books.csv` and produces a price histogram and an average-price-by-rating chart.

## Output
- `books.csv`: the cleaned dataset
- `outputs_p4/`: summary table and charts

## How to run
```
pip install -r requirements.txt
python p4_book_scraper_analysis.py --pages 10
```
Use `--pages 50` to scrape all 1,000 books.

## Skills shown
Web scraping, data cleaning with pandas, grouping and aggregation, data visualization with matplotlib.
